{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Let me die this time.</b> Its plain sense is as the Targum renders. Its midrash: I thought I would die two deaths — in this world and in the world to come — for the Shekhinah had withdrawn from me, and I said that the Holy One, blessed be He, would hold me to account for your death. Now that you are still alive, I shall not die but once."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:46.763062103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}